# Governance Proposal: Inject current time into Kart system prompt

**Proposer:** Ganesha (Claude Code CLI / Sonnet 4.6)
**Date:** 2026-02-25T18:56:20Z
**Type:** Bug Fix
**Trust Level:** ENGINEER (3)

## Summary
Free-tier LLMs called by kart_orchestrator._build_system_prompt() have no knowledge of the current date or time. Any timestamps they generate (governance proposals, session records, etc.) default to 00:00 or are entirely fabricated. Fix: inject datetime.now().isoformat() into the system prompt so every LLM call has accurate time context. datetime is already imported in kart_orchestrator.py.

## Proposed Changes

### File: core/kart_orchestrator.py

**Change:** In _build_system_prompt(), add current time to the agent context block at the end of the prompt.

Change from:
```python
Current user: {self.username}
Your trust level: ENGINEER
Session: {self.session_id}

Be direct and practical. Focus on execution, not explanation."""
```

To:
```python
Current user: {self.username}
Your trust level: ENGINEER
Session: {self.session_id}
Current time: {datetime.now().isoformat()}

Be direct and practical. Focus on execution, not explanation."""
```

## Rationale
- datetime is already imported at the top of kart_orchestrator.py — zero new dependencies
- Every LLM prompt now contains the actual wall-clock time at invocation
- Governance proposals, session logs, and any timestamps the LLM generates will be accurate
- One line, one string interpolation

## Risk Assessment
- **Risk Level:** MINIMAL
- **Reversible:** YES — remove one line
- **Dependencies:** datetime (already imported)
- **Testing:** Ask Kart to write a proposal — check the timestamp matches real time

## ΔE Impact
Expected ΔE: +0.005 (eliminates timestamp fabrication from all Kart-generated content)

